# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Introduction {#introduction}"
msgstr "Panimula {#introduction}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A Fourier transform is a ubiquitous tool with applications in math, physics,"
" signal processing, data compression, and countless other fields. A "
"*quantum* version of the Fourier transform, aptly named the quantum Fourier "
"transform, forms the basis for some of the most important quantum "
"algorithms.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Fourier transform ay isang ubiquitous na kasangkapan na may mga "
"aplikasyon sa matematika, pisika, signal processing, data compression, at "
"napakaraming iba pang larangan. Ang *quantum* na bersyon ng Fourier "
"transform, na angkop na pinangalanang quantum Fourier transform, ang "
"pundasyon ng ilan sa mga pinakamahalagang quantum algorithm.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Today, after a reminder of the classical Fourier transform, we'll talk about"
" how we implement the quantum Fourier transform on a quantum computer. Then,"
" we'll discuss one of the applications of the quantum Fourier transform to "
"an algorithm called the phase estimation algorithm. Quantum phase estimation"
" is a subroutine in Shor's famous factoring algorithm, which is sometimes "
"referred to as the \"crown jewel\" of quantum computing. This module builds "
"toward another module all about Shor's algorithm, but it's also meant to be "
"stand-alone. The quantum Fourier transform is a fascinating and useful "
"algorithm in its own right!\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, pagkatapos ng isang paalala tungkol sa klasikal na Fourier "
"transform, pag-uusapan natin kung paano natin isinasagawa ang quantum "
"Fourier transform sa isang quantum computer. Pagkatapos, tatalakayin natin "
"ang isa sa mga aplikasyon ng quantum Fourier transform sa isang algorithm na"
" tinatawag na phase estimation algorithm. Ang quantum phase estimation ay "
"isang subroutine sa sikat na factoring algorithm ni Shor, na kung minsan ay "
"tinutukoy bilang \"crown jewel\" ng quantum computing. Ang module na ito ay "
"nagtatayo patungo sa isa pang module tungkol sa Shor's algorithm, ngunit "
"nilalayon din itong maging nagsasarili. Ang quantum Fourier transform ay "
"isang kahanga-hangang at kapaki-pakinabang na algorithm sa sarili nito!\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The classical Fourier transform {#the-classical-fourier-transform}"
msgstr "Ang klasikal na Fourier transform {#the-classical-fourier-transform}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Before we jump into the quantum Fourier transform, let's first remind "
"ourselves of the classical version. The Fourier transform is a method of "
"transforming from one so-called \"basis\" to another. You can think of two "
"bases as different perspectives of the same problem — they are both valid "
"ways to express a function, but one or the other might be more illuminating,"
" depending on the problem at hand. Some examples of pairs of bases that are "
"connected by Fourier transform are position and momentum, and time and "
"frequency.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bago tayo sumabak sa quantum Fourier transform, unahin nating alalahanin ang"
" klasikal na bersyon. Ang Fourier transform ay isang paraan ng pag-transform"
" mula sa isang tinatawag na \"basis\" patungo sa isa pa. Maaari mong isipin "
"ang dalawang basis bilang iba't ibang pananaw ng parehong problema — "
"parehong may bisa na paraan upang ipahayag ang isang function, ngunit ang "
"isa o ang isa pa ay maaaring mas kapaki-pakinabang, depende sa problemang "
"nararapit. Ilang halimbawa ng mga pares ng basis na konektado ng Fourier "
"transform ay posisyon at momentum, at oras at dalas.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's see an example of how the Fourier transform might help us figure out "
"what note an instrument is playing based on its audio waveform. Typically, "
"we see the waveforms represented in the time basis — that is, the amplitude "
"of the wave is expressed as a function of time.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tingnan natin ang isang halimbawa kung paano ang Fourier transform ay "
"makakatulong sa atin na malaman kung anong nota ang tinutugtog ng isang "
"instrumento batay sa audio waveform nito. Karaniwan, nakikita natin ang mga "
"waveform na kinakatawan sa time basis — iyon ay, ang amplitude ng alon ay "
"ipinahahayag bilang isang function ng oras.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Single sinusoidal signal plotted as a function of "
"time.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/Cnote.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Isang solong sinusoidal na signal na naka-plot bilang function ng "
"oras.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/Cnote.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can Fourier transform this waveform to go from the time basis to the "
"frequency basis:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari tayong mag-Fourier transform ng waveform na ito para lumipat mula sa "
"time basis patungo sa frequency basis:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Frequency spectrum of the audio waveform. One clear sharp peak at 260 "
"Hz.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/Cnotefreq.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Frequency spectrum ng audio waveform. Isang malinaw na matalas na tuktok "
"sa 260 Hz.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/Cnotefreq.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the frequency basis, we can easily see a clear peak at about 260 Hz. "
"That's a middle C!\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa frequency basis, madali tayong makakakita ng malinaw na tuktok sa "
"humigit-kumulang 260 Hz. Iyon ay isang middle C!\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, you might have been able to determine that a middle C was being played "
"without the use of a Fourier transform, but what if multiple notes are "
"played at once? Then the waveform becomes more complicated when we plot it "
"in the time basis:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngayon, maaaring nagawa mong matukoy na ang isang middle C ay tinutugtog "
"nang hindi gumagamit ng Fourier transform, ngunit paano kung maraming nota "
"ang tinutugtog nang sabay-sabay? Ang waveform ay nagiging mas kumplikado "
"kapag ini-plot natin ito sa time basis:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Displacement versus time graph of multiple sine waves at once, creating a "
"more complicated periodic pattern.](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/qft/Cchord.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Displacement versus time graph ng maraming sine wave nang sabay-sabay, na "
"lumilikha ng mas kumplikadong periodic na "
"pattern.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/Cchord.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "But the frequency spectrum clearly identifies three peaks:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngunit ang frequency spectrum ay malinaw na nagtatukoy ng tatlong tuktok:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Frequency spectrum of the above audio waveform. Three peaks at "
"approximately 260 Hz, 330 Hz, and 392 Hz. The last peak is very weak, but "
"visible.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/Cchordfreq.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Frequency spectrum ng nasa itaas na audio waveform. Tatlong tuktok sa "
"humigit-kumulang 260 Hz, 330 Hz, at 392 Hz. Ang huling tuktok ay napakahina,"
" ngunit nakikita.](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/qft/Cchordfreq.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "This was a C-major chord, playing the notes C, E, and G.\n"
msgstr "Ito ay isang C-major chord, na tumutugtog ng mga nota C, E, at G.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This kind of Fourier analysis can help us extract the frequency components "
"of any sort of complicated signal.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang ganitong uri ng Fourier analysis ay makakatulong sa atin na kunin ang "
"mga frequency component ng anumang uri ng kumplikadong signal.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Discrete Fourier transform {#discrete-fourier-transform}"
msgstr "Discrete Fourier transform {#discrete-fourier-transform}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Fourier transform is useful for any number of signal-processing "
"applications. But in most of these real-world applications (including the "
"music example we used above), we want to transform a discrete set of $N$ "
"data points — not a continuous function. In this case, we use the *discrete*"
" Fourier transform. The discrete Fourier transform (DFT) acts on a vector "
"$(x_0, ..., x_{N-1})$ and maps it to the vector $(y_0, ..., y_{N-1})$ "
"according to the formula:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Fourier transform ay kapaki-pakinabang para sa anumang bilang ng mga "
"aplikasyon sa signal-processing. Ngunit sa karamihan ng mga totoong "
"aplikasyon na ito (kasama ang halimbawa ng musika na ginamit natin sa "
"itaas), gusto nating i-transform ang isang discrete na hanay ng $N$ data "
"points — hindi isang tuloy-tuloy na function. Sa kasong ito, ginagamit natin"
" ang *discrete* Fourier transform. Ang discrete Fourier transform (DFT) ay "
"kumikilos sa isang vector $(x_0, ..., x_{N-1})$ at ini-map ito sa vector "
"$(y_0, ..., y_{N-1})$ ayon sa formula:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$y_k = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}}\\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}x_j\\omega_N^{jk}$$\n"
msgstr "$$y_k = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}}\\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}x_j\\omega_N^{jk}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where we take $\\omega_N^{jk} = e^{2\\pi i \\frac{jk}{N}}$. (Note that there"
" are other conventions that have a minus sign in the exponential, so be "
"careful when you see the DFT in the wild.) Recall that $e^{2\\pi i "
"\\frac{jk}{N}}$ is a periodic function, with period $\\frac{N}{k}$. So, by "
"multiplying by this function, the Fourier transform is essentially a way to "
"break the (discrete) function $\\{x_{j}\\}$ into a linear combination of its"
" constituent periodic functions, each with period $\\frac{N}{k}$.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan kinukuha natin ang $\\omega_N^{jk} = e^{2\\pi i \\frac{jk}{N}}$. "
"(Tandaan na may iba pang mga convention na may negatibong tanda sa "
"exponential, kaya mag-ingat kapag nakita mo ang DFT sa labas.) Alalahanin na"
" ang $e^{2\\pi i \\frac{jk}{N}}$ ay isang periodic na function, na may "
"period na $\\frac{N}{k}$. Kaya, sa pamamagitan ng pagpaparami ng function na"
" ito, ang Fourier transform ay essentially isang paraan upang masira ang "
"(discrete) function na $\\{x_{j}\\}$ sa isang linear na kumbinasyon ng mga "
"bumubuo nitong periodic na function, bawat isa ay may period na "
"$\\frac{N}{k}$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The quantum Fourier transform {#the-quantum-fourier-transform}"
msgstr "Ang quantum Fourier transform {#the-quantum-fourier-transform}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So now, we've seen how the Fourier transform is used to represent a function"
" as a linear combination of a new set of so-called \"basis functions.\" "
"Basis transformations are regularly done on qubit states, too. For example, "
"the state of a single qubit $|\\psi\\rangle$ can be expressed in the "
"computational basis $|\\psi\\rangle = c_0 |0\\rangle + c_1 |1\\rangle$, with"
" basis states $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$, or in the $X$ basis "
"$|\\psi\\rangle = c_+ |+\\rangle + c_- |-\\rangle$ with basis states "
"$|+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$ and "
"$|-\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (|0\\rangle - |1\\rangle)$. Both are "
"equally valid, but one might be more natural than the other, depending on "
"the type of problem you are trying to solve.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya ngayon, nakita na natin kung paano ginagamit ang Fourier transform "
"upang kumatawan sa isang function bilang isang linear na kumbinasyon ng "
"isang bagong hanay ng tinatawag na \"basis functions.\" Ang mga basis "
"transformation ay regular na ginagawa rin sa mga estado ng qubit. Halimbawa,"
" ang estado ng isang solong qubit $|\\psi\\rangle$ ay maaaring ipahayag sa "
"computational basis $|\\psi\\rangle = c_0 |0\\rangle + c_1 |1\\rangle$, na "
"may mga basis state na $|0\\rangle$ at $|1\\rangle$, o sa $X$ basis "
"$|\\psi\\rangle = c_+ |+\\rangle + c_- |-\\rangle$ na may mga basis state na"
" $|+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (|0\\rangle + |1\\rangle)$ at "
"$|-\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} (|0\\rangle - |1\\rangle)$. Parehong may "
"pantay na bisa, ngunit ang isa ay maaaring mas natural kaysa sa isa, depende"
" sa uri ng problemang sinusubukan mong lutasin.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Qubit states can also be expressed in the Fourier basis where a state is "
"expressed in terms of a linear combination of the Fourier basis states "
"$|\\phi_y\\rangle$, rather than the usual, computational basis states, "
"$|x\\rangle$. To do this, you need to apply a quantum Fourier transform "
"(QFT):\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga estado ng qubit ay maaari ring ipahayag sa Fourier basis kung saan "
"ang isang estado ay ipinahahayag sa mga tuntunin ng isang linear na "
"kumbinasyon ng mga Fourier basis state na $|\\phi_y\\rangle$, sa halip na "
"ang karaniwang mga computational basis state na $|x\\rangle$. Upang magawa "
"ito, kailangan mong mag-apply ng quantum Fourier transform (QFT):\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$ | \\phi_y \\rangle =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}}\\sum_{x=0}^{N-1}\\omega_N^{y "
"x} \\vert x \\rangle$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$ | \\phi_y \\rangle =  \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{N}}\\sum_{x=0}^{N-1}\\omega_N^{y "
"x} \\vert x \\rangle$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"with $\\omega_N^{yx} = e^{\\frac{2\\pi i y x}{N}}$ as above, and $N$ is the "
"number of basis states in your quantum system. Note that, since we're "
"working with qubits now, $m$ qubits gives you $2^m$ basis states, so "
"$N=2^m$. Here, the basis states are written as a single number $|x\\rangle$ "
"where $x$ ranges from $0$ to $N-1$, but you might more typically see the "
"basis states expressed as $|00...00\\rangle$, $|00...01\\rangle$, "
"$|00...11\\rangle$, ..., $|11...11\\rangle$, where each binary digit "
"represents the state of qubit 0 through $m-1$, from right to left. There's "
"an easy way to convert these binary states to a single number: simply treat "
"them like binary numbers! So, $|00...00\\rangle = |0\\rangle$, "
"$|00...01\\rangle = |1\\rangle$, $|00...10\\rangle = |2\\rangle$, "
"$|00...11\\rangle = |3\\rangle$, and so on, all the way up to  "
"$|11...11\\rangle = |2^m -1\\rangle = |N-1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"na may $\\omega_N^{yx} = e^{\\frac{2\\pi i y x}{N}}$ tulad ng nasa itaas, at"
" $N$ ang bilang ng mga basis state sa iyong quantum system. Tandaan na, "
"dahil nagtatrabaho tayo ngayon sa mga qubit, ang $m$ qubit ay nagbibigay sa "
"iyo ng $2^m$ na mga basis state, kaya $N=2^m$. Dito, ang mga basis state ay "
"nakasulat bilang isang solong numero $|x\\rangle$ kung saan ang $x$ ay "
"umaabot mula $0$ hanggang $N-1$, ngunit mas madalas mong makikita ang mga "
"basis state na ipinahahayag bilang $|00...00\\rangle$, $|00...01\\rangle$, "
"$|00...11\\rangle$, ..., $|11...11\\rangle$, kung saan ang bawat binary "
"digit ay kumakatawan sa estado ng qubit 0 hanggang $m-1$, mula kanan "
"hanggang kaliwa. May madaling paraan upang i-convert ang mga binary state na"
" ito sa isang solong numero: ituring lamang silang mga binary number! Kaya, "
"$|00...00\\rangle = |0\\rangle$, $|00...01\\rangle = |1\\rangle$, "
"$|00...10\\rangle = |2\\rangle$, $|00...11\\rangle = |3\\rangle$, at iba pa,"
" hanggang sa $|11...11\\rangle = |2^m -1\\rangle = |N-1\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Build intuition for the Fourier basis states {#build-intuition-for-the-"
"fourier-basis-states}"
msgstr ""
"Bumuo ng intuition para sa mga Fourier basis state {#build-intuition-for-"
"the-fourier-basis-states}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, we've just gone over what the computational basis states are and how "
"they're ordered: they're the set of states where each qubit is either in $0$"
" or $1$, and we order them from the state where all qubits are $0$, "
"$|00...00\\rangle$, to the state where they are all $1$, "
"$|11...11\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, napag-usapan na natin kung ano ang mga computational basis state at "
"kung paano sila inayos: sila ang hanay ng mga estado kung saan ang bawat "
"qubit ay nasa $0$ o $1$, at inayos natin sila mula sa estado kung saan ang "
"lahat ng qubit ay $0$, $|00...00\\rangle$, hanggang sa estado kung saan ang "
"lahat ay $1$, $|11...11\\rangle$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"But how can we make sense of the *Fourier* basis states? All of the Fourier "
"basis states are equal superpositions of all the computational basis states,"
" but each state differs from the other in the periodicity in the components'"
" *phase*. To understand this more concretely, let's take a look at the four "
"Fourier basis states of a two-qubit system. The lowest Fourier state is one "
"whose phase does not vary at all:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ngunit paano natin mauunawaan ang mga *Fourier* basis state? Lahat ng "
"Fourier basis state ay magkaparehong superposition ng lahat ng computational"
" basis state, ngunit ang bawat estado ay naiiba sa isa pa sa periodicity ng "
"*phase* ng mga component. Upang maunawaan ito nang mas kongkreto, tingnan "
"natin ang apat na Fourier basis state ng isang two-Qubit system. Ang "
"pinakamababang Fourier state ay ang isa na ang phase ay hindi nagbabago:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle + |10\\rangle +"
" |11\\rangle)$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$|\\phi_0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle + |01\\rangle + |10\\rangle +"
" |11\\rangle)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can visualize this state by plotting the complex amplitude of each of the"
" terms. The red line guides the eye to show you how the phase of this "
"amplitude winds around the complex plane as a function of the computational "
"basis state. For $|\\phi_0\\rangle$, the phase remains constant:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari nating i-visualize ang estado na ito sa pamamagitan ng pag-plot ng "
"complex amplitude ng bawat isa sa mga term. Ang pulang linya ay nagbibigay-"
"gabay sa mata upang ipakita sa iyo kung paano ang phase ng amplitude na ito "
"ay nagpapaikot sa paligid ng complex plane bilang isang function ng "
"computational basis state. Para sa $|\\phi_0\\rangle$, ang phase ay "
"nananatiling constant:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bar graph of the complex amplitude (x-y plane) for each computational "
"basis state (z-axis) for $phi_0$. They are all real, and so the bars all "
"point to +1 on the x-axis](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/qft/phi0.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Bar graph ng complex amplitude (x-y plane) para sa bawat computational "
"basis state (z-axis) para sa $phi_0$. Lahat sila ay real, kaya ang mga bar "
"ay nakaturo lahat sa +1 sa x-axis](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/qft/phi0.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The next Fourier basis state is the one whose components' phases wind around"
" from $0$ to $2\\pi$ just once:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang susunod na Fourier basis state ay ang isa na ang mga phase ng mga "
"component ay nagpapaikot mula $0$ hanggang $2\\pi$ nang isang beses "
"lamang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$|\\phi_1\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle + e^{i\\pi/2}|01\\rangle + "
"e^{i\\pi}|10\\rangle + e^{3i\\pi/2}|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2}(|00\\rangle +"
" i|01\\rangle - |10\\rangle - i|11\\rangle)$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$|\\phi_1\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle + e^{i\\pi/2}|01\\rangle + "
"e^{i\\pi}|10\\rangle + e^{3i\\pi/2}|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2}(|00\\rangle +"
" i|01\\rangle - |10\\rangle - i|11\\rangle)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And we can see this winding in the plot of complex amplitude versus "
"computational basis state:\n"
msgstr ""
"At makikita natin ang pag-ikot na ito sa plot ng complex amplitude versus "
"computational basis state:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bar graph of the complex amplitude (x-y plane) for each computational "
"basis state (z-axis) for $phi_1$. The red line shows how the complex phase "
"accumulates such that it winds around $2\\pi$ once as you step through all "
"of the computational basis states.](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/qft/phi1.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Bar graph ng complex amplitude (x-y plane) para sa bawat computational "
"basis state (z-axis) para sa $phi_1$. Ang pulang linya ay nagpapakita kung "
"paano nag-aakumula ang complex phase na nagpapaikot ng $2\\pi$ nang isang "
"beses habang ikaw ay humahakbang sa lahat ng computational basis "
"state.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/phi1.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, each state has a phase that is $2\\pi/4$ radians higher than the state "
"before it when they're ordered in the standard way, since in this example we"
" have four basis states ($N=4$). The next basis state winds around from 0 to"
" 2$\\pi$ twice:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kaya, ang bawat estado ay may phase na $2\\pi/4$ radians na mas mataas kaysa"
" sa estado bago ito kapag inayos sila sa karaniwang paraan, dahil sa "
"halimbawang ito ay mayroon tayong apat na basis state ($N=4$). Ang susunod "
"na basis state ay nagpapaikot mula 0 hanggang $2\\pi$ nang dalawang beses:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$|\\phi_2\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle + e^{i\\pi}|01\\rangle + "
"e^{2i\\pi}|10\\rangle + e^{3i\\pi}|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle -"
" |01\\rangle + |10\\rangle - |11\\rangle)$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$|\\phi_2\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle + e^{i\\pi}|01\\rangle + "
"e^{2i\\pi}|10\\rangle + e^{3i\\pi}|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle -"
" |01\\rangle + |10\\rangle - |11\\rangle)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bar graph of the complex amplitude (x-y plane) for each computational "
"basis state (z-axis) for $phi_2$. The red line shows how the complex phase "
"accumulates such that it winds around $2\\pi$ twice as you step through all "
"of the computational basis states.](/learning/images/modules/computer-"
"science/qft/phi2.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Bar graph ng complex amplitude (x-y plane) para sa bawat computational "
"basis state (z-axis) para sa $phi_2$. Ang pulang linya ay nagpapakita kung "
"paano nag-aakumula ang complex phase na nagpapaikot ng $2\\pi$ nang dalawang"
" beses habang ikaw ay humahakbang sa lahat ng computational basis "
"state.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/phi2.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Finally, the highest Fourier component is the one with the fastest varying "
"phase. For our example with two qubits, it's the one whose phases wind "
"around from 0 to $2\\pi$ three times:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa wakas, ang pinakamataas na Fourier component ay ang isa na may "
"pinakamabilis na nagbabagong phase. Para sa ating halimbawa na may dalawang "
"qubit, ito ang isa na ang mga phase ay nagpapaikot mula 0 hanggang $2\\pi$ "
"nang tatlong beses:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$|\\phi_3\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle + e^{3i\\pi/2}|01\\rangle + "
"e^{6i\\pi/2}|10\\rangle + e^{9i\\pi/2}|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2} "
"(|00\\rangle - i|01\\rangle - |10\\rangle + i|11\\rangle)$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$|\\phi_3\\rangle = \\frac{1}{2} (|00\\rangle + e^{3i\\pi/2}|01\\rangle + "
"e^{6i\\pi/2}|10\\rangle + e^{9i\\pi/2}|11\\rangle) = \\frac{1}{2} "
"(|00\\rangle - i|01\\rangle - |10\\rangle + i|11\\rangle)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Bar graph of the complex amplitude (x-y plane) for each computational "
"basis state (z-axis) for $phi_3$. The red line shows how the complex phase "
"accumulates such that it winds around $2\\pi$ three times as you step "
"through all of the computational basis "
"states.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/phi3.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Bar graph ng complex amplitude (x-y plane) para sa bawat computational "
"basis state (z-axis) para sa $phi_3$. Ang pulang linya ay nagpapakita kung "
"paano nag-aakumula ang complex phase na nagpapaikot ng $2\\pi$ nang tatlong "
"beses habang ikaw ay humahakbang sa lahat ng computational basis "
"state.](/learning/images/modules/computer-science/qft/phi3.avif)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In general, for an $m$-qubit state, there will be $2^m$ Fourier basis "
"states, whose frequency in phase variation ranges from constant, for "
"$|\\phi_0\\rangle$, to rapidly varying for $|\\phi_{2^m-1}\\rangle$, "
"completing $2^m-1$ windings around $2\\pi$ over the superposition of states."
" So, when we take a QFT of a quantum state, we're essentially doing the same"
" basic analysis that we did for the musical waveform in the Intro. We're "
"determining the Fourier frequency components that contribute to creating the"
" quantum state of interest.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa pangkalahatan, para sa isang $m$-Qubit na estado, magkakaroon ng $2^m$ "
"Fourier basis state, na ang dalas ng pagbabago ng phase ay umaabot mula sa "
"constant, para sa $|\\phi_0\\rangle$, hanggang sa mabilis na nagbabago para "
"sa $|\\phi_{2^m-1}\\rangle$, kumukumpleto ng $2^m-1$ na pag-ikot sa paligid "
"ng $2\\pi$ sa superposition ng mga estado. Kaya, kapag kinukuha natin ang "
"QFT ng isang quantum state, essentially ginagawa natin ang parehong "
"pangunahing pagsusuri na ginawa natin para sa musical waveform sa Panimula. "
"Tinutukoy natin ang mga Fourier frequency component na nag-aambag sa "
"paglikha ng quantum state ng interes.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Try some example QFTs {#try-some-example-qfts}"
msgstr "Subukan ang ilang halimbawang QFT {#try-some-example-qfts}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's try to continue to build our intuition for the quantum Fourier "
"transform by making a state in the computational basis, then seeing what "
"happens when we apply the QFT to it. For now, we'll just treat the QFT as a "
"black box that we apply using the `QFTGate` from the [Qiskit circuit "
"library.](/guides/circuit-library) Later, we'll take a peak under the hood "
"to see how it's implemented.\n"
msgstr ""
"Subukan nating patuloy na buuin ang ating intuition para sa quantum Fourier "
"transform sa pamamagitan ng paggawa ng isang estado sa computational basis, "
"at pagkatapos ay tingnan kung ano ang mangyayari kapag inilapat natin ang "
"QFT dito. Sa ngayon, ituring nating isang black box ang QFT na inilalapat "
"natin gamit ang `QFTGate` mula sa [Qiskit circuit library.](/guides/circuit-"
"library) Mamaya, titingnan natin ang loob nito upang makita kung paano ito "
"isinasagawa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We start by loading the necessary packages and selecting a device to run our"
" circuit on:\n"
msgstr ""
"Sisimulan natin sa pamamagitan ng pag-load ng mga kinakailangang package at "
"pagpili ng isang device para patakbuhin ang ating circuit:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If you don't have time available on your account or want to use a simulator "
"for any reason, you can run the cell below to set up a simulator that will "
"mimic the quantum device we selected above:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung wala kang available na oras sa iyong account o nais gumamit ng "
"simulator sa anumang dahilan, maaari mong patakbuhin ang cell sa ibaba para "
"mag-set up ng simulator na magpapalita ng quantum device na pinili natin sa "
"itaas:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ####
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Single computational basis state {#single-computational-basis-state}"
msgstr "Isang computational basis state {#single-computational-basis-state}"

